{title: ’Tis So Sweet to Trust in Jesus}
{artist: Louisa M. R. Stead (1850-1917)}
{key: G}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[G]’Tis so sweet to [C]trust in [G]Jesus,
[Em]Just to take Him [D]at His word;
[G]Just to rest up[C]on His [G]promise,
[Em]Just to know, Thus [D]saith the [G]Lord.
{eov}

{soc}
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]how I [G]trust Him!
[Em]How I’ve proved Him [D]o’er and o’er!
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]precious [G]Jesus!
[Em]O for grace to [D]trust Him [G]more!
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 2}
[G]O how sweet to [C]trust in [G]Jesus,
[Em]Just to trust His [D]cleansing blood;
[G]Just in simple [C]faith to [G]plunge me
[Em]’Neath the healing, [D]cleansing [G]flood.
{eov}

{soc}
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]how I [G]trust Him!
[Em]How I’ve proved Him [D]o’er and o’er!
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]precious [G]Jesus!
[Em]O for grace to [D]trust Him [G]more!
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 3}
[G]Yes, ’tis sweet to [C]trust in [G]Jesus,
[Em]Just from sin and [D]self to cease;
[G]Just from Jesus [C]simply [G]taking
[Em]Life and rest, and [D]joy and [G]peace.
{eov}

{soc}
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]how I [G]trust Him!
[Em]How I’ve proved Him [D]o’er and o’er!
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]precious [G]Jesus!
[Em]O for grace to [D]trust Him [G]more!
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 4}
[G]I’m so glad I [C]learned to [G]trust Thee,
[Em]Precious Jesus, [D]Savior, Friend;
[G]And I know that [C]Thou art [G]with me,
[Em]Wilt be with me [D]to the [G]end.
{eov}

{soc}
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]how I [G]trust Him!
[Em]How I’ve proved Him [D]o’er and o’er!
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]precious [G]Jesus!
[Em]O for grace to [D]trust Him [G]more!
{eoc}
